  {% set sailyPrimary = providerB.codes | findCode(providerB.primaryCode) %}

  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Pick <strong>Holafly</strong> for a flat unlimited price with no gigabyte counting at all. Pick <strong>Saily</strong> if you want to pay per GB but get a real security bundle (ad blocking, malware blocking, a virtual-location tool) thrown in, since it's built by NordVPN's parent company. Both were blocked from new purchases in Turkey by the country's telecom regulator starting mid-2025, so that's a wash either way if Turkey's on the itinerary.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: Unlimited Flat Rate vs. Metered Plus Security Bundle</h2>
  <p>
    Holafly's entire pitch is not having to think about data: one flat price per day, per country or region, and it just keeps working. Saily prices by the gigabyte instead, which is usually cheaper for a light user, but every Saily plan bundles in ad blocking, malware and phishing site blocking, and a virtual-location tool as standard, not an add-on. If you'd normally pay for a VPN separately when traveling, that's already priced into a Saily plan.
  </p>
  <p>
    Saily also sells one universal eSIM that keeps working as you cross into a new supported country, rather than a separate profile per destination. Holafly plans are scoped to the specific country or region you buy, so a multi-country trip covering destinations outside that region needs a new plan.
  </p>

